 @robaitken4592  Yeah in terms of idle power AMD is quite awful, Ryzen's idle consumption is so high that it doesn't make sense (in Europe) to use Ryzen for servers who will be mostly idle i.e. NAS systems etc. 
I don't know why their GPU's are so bad in idle though, with Ryzen it's the IO die and the chiplet architecture that's terribly inefficient @idle.
Just to give you an example, a laptop 7945HX idles at 30W, in a laptop that's really really rough.
